ALIAS(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    alias - define shell command aliases

SYNOPSIS
    alias [name[=value]...]
    unalias name...

DESCRIPTION
    With no arguments, lists aliases. name=value sets an alias, and name
    alone displays it. unalias removes named aliases. Quote values containing
    spaces. An alias is expanded when the shell executes a simple command;
    nested expansion is limited to sixteen levels. /etc/profile defines
    ll='ls -lh' and la='ls -a' for interactive shells.

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), man(1), index(7)
